entry.content:
kyreos_dmarc_audit_tool: description, title, annotations  -Live DNS check of any +Email validation for a +MX, SPF and -policy, SPF +records are checked, scored and explained, -recursive lookup count against -RFC 7208 limit of 10, DKIM probed at 10 common selectors (custom selectors may be missed), MX. Returns a 0-100 score, issues, and the exact next DMARC record +fix -publish, keeping sp, ruf and fo. For agents that send mail as a domain. +make.
kyreos_dns_check: description, title, inputSchema, annotations  -DNS lookup +Domain lookup: A, MX, TXT and NS records -agents: query A, AAAA, MX, TXT, NS, CNAME, SOA, CAA, SRV or PTR records through Cloudflare and Google at once. Returns the records, whether the two resolvers agree, and whether DNSSEC validated. +any domain as JSON, live. -{"name":"example.com","type":"MX"}. +{"domain":"example.com"}.  parameters: -{"name":"example.com","type":"MX"} +{"domain":"example.com"}
kyreos_x402_precheck: description, title, inputSchema, annotations  -Give it an -URL. It reads the live 402 envelope, +payment endpoint test: checks that a paid route answers, quotes a valid 402, has a sane price and a real -price, network and asset, then checks the payee's settlement history in a chain-stamped index (payer count and last settlement are host-level). Returns PAY or a reason not to. 0.002 USDC, a fifth of the 0.01 endpoint-lint checks, plus chain proof. +all before your agent pays. -?url=https://host/paid-route. +{"url":"https://host/route"}.  parameters: -?url=https://host/paid-route +{"url":"https://host/route"}
